<title>USA: Intl Standards sets 1 to 15 reverse split.</title>
<headline>Intl Standards sets 1 to 15 reverse split.</headline>
<dateline>BOCA RATON, Fla. 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>International Standards Group Ltd said Wednesday that it setting a 1 to 15 reverse stock split which reduces its outstanding common stock to about six million shares, with about 2.5 million in the public float.</p>
<p>The company said it is also changing its name to &quot;Total World Telecommunications Inc&quot; effective immediately, and changing its trading symbol to &quot;TWTI.&quot;</p>
<p>-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
</text>
